Subject: Drain failed native raw reads before releasing optional whole-file owners

Upstream-base: f1e9646a7da6950143e77b1daed33a92c931a638

A raw range read has no whole-file registry entry. Cancel the failed logical
request and its paired tail so external NL servicing cannot leave it pending
forever. Join workers before optional whole-file storage is released, preserve
unrelated reads, and propagate the original I/O failure without callbacks.

diff --git a/src/NL/nlFileGC.cpp b/src/NL/nlFileGC.cpp
--- a/src/NL/nlFileGC.cpp
+++ b/src/NL/nlFileGC.cpp
@@ -492,9 +492,12 @@
         }
         catch (...)
         {
-            // Drop only this whole-file request. Its owned file drains the raw
-            // entries before its destination is freed; unrelated loads survive.
-            nlAbortEntireFileLoad(entry->m_pFile);
+            // Remove this logical raw request, including its paired tail, before
+            // an optional whole-file owner releases the destination and file.
+            // Raw range reads have no whole-file owner; unrelated reads survive.
+            auto* failedFile = entry->m_pFile;
+            CancelNative(entry, 0);
+            nlAbortEntireFileLoad(failedFile);
             throw;
         }
         if (tail)
